   "daf": "21b",
   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "עַד שֶׁתִּכְלֶה רֶגֶל מִן הַשּׁוּק. וְעַד כַּמָּה? אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: עַד דְּכָלְיָא רִיגְלָא דְתַרְמוֹדָאֵי.",
   "en": "The expression «until traffic in the marketplace ceases» is mentioned here, and the Gemara asks: «Until when» exactly is this time? «Rabba bar bar Ḥana said» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan said: Until» the «traffic of» the people of «Tadmor [tarmoda’ei] ceases.» They sold kindling wood and remained in the marketplace later than everyone else. People who discovered at sunset that they had exhausted their wood supply could purchase wood from them."
  }
